Changes from the upstream files
-------------------------------

Copyright (C) 2026 Isak Sky. The changes are licensed under Apache-2.0.

* The parts used are rewritten in C# as one internal class,
  PdfCartonJpegSamples, which decodes a whole JPEG held in memory to its
  stored component samples with no colour conversion. The libjpeg API,
  its object and memory managers, source managers, error handling and
  suspension are not ported.
* Only baseline, extended sequential and progressive Huffman decoding of
  8-bit samples is kept, with restart intervals: from jdhuff.c and
  jdphuff.c, Huffman table derivation and checks, DC and AC decoding,
  progressive AC refinement and end-of-band runs, and the zero coefficients
  used after the entropy-coded data runs out; from jdmarker.c and
  jdinput.c, marker and frame checks, component dimensions, quantization
  table latching and restart resynchronization. Arithmetic, lossless and
  hierarchical decoding, 12- and 16-bit samples, DNL heights and fractional
  sampling ratios are not ported; the decoder returns no result for them.
* Huffman decoding uses a 9-bit lookahead table and a 64-bit bit buffer in
  place of libjpeg's 8-bit lookahead and bit-reading macros.
* From jidctint.c, only the 8x8 jpeg_idct_islow is kept, with its passes
  written as one shared routine; output range limiting uses a 1024-entry
  table in place of jdmaster.c's range-limit table. The other IDCT sizes and
  methods are not ported.
* From jdsample.c, the h2v1, h2v2 and h1v2 triangle-filter ("fancy")
  upsampling and the integral replication upsampling are kept, written over
  whole rows; merged upsampling and colour conversion are not ported.
* From jdcoefct.c, smoothing_ok and decompress_smooth_data's 5x5 block
  smoothing for incomplete progressive images are kept, applied after all
  scans are read rather than per iMCU row; coefficient and sample buffers
  come from System.Buffers.ArrayPool.
* From jutils.c, the natural-order table with its 16 extra entries is kept.
